"The web server is Nginx, that ignores the files \".htaccess\": the sensitive "
"directories of \"files/\" (backup, import, userdata…) are public and the "
"rules of the modules are not applied. Configure them in the config of Nginx."
msgstr ""

#: src/Stdlib/HtaccessAudit.php:47
msgid ""
"The module {module} requires a rewrite of \"files/\" to \"{route}\" in the "
"config of Nginx, for example: {example}"
msgstr ""

#: src/Stdlib/HtaccessAudit.php:57
msgid ""
"The web server is \"{server}\": check that it applies the files "
"\".htaccess\" of Omeka and of \"files/\", else configure the protections in "
"its own config."
msgstr ""

#: src/Stdlib/HtaccessAudit.php:63
msgid ""
"The file \".htaccess\" is missing at the root of Omeka: the urls and the "
"protections do not work."
msgstr ""

#: src/Stdlib/HtaccessAudit.php:97
msgid ""
"The file \".htaccess\" does not enable the rewrite engine (\"RewriteEngine "
"On\"): the urls of Omeka do not work."
msgstr ""

#: src/Stdlib/HtaccessAudit.php:110
msgid ""
"The module Access is active, but the file \".htaccess\" has no rule to "
"redirect \"files/\" to it: the files are not protected."
msgstr ""

#: src/Stdlib/HtaccessAudit.php:111
msgid ""
"The module Analytics is active, but the file \".htaccess\" has no rule to "
"redirect \"files/\" to it: the downloads are not counted."
msgstr ""

#: src/Stdlib/HtaccessAudit.php:121
msgid ""
"The file \".htaccess\" redirects the files {types} to the module {module} "
"(line {line}), that is not active: these files are not available."
msgstr ""

#: src/Stdlib/HtaccessAudit.php:128
msgid ""
"The rule of the module {module} (line {line}) is placed after the rule that "
"serves the existing files directly (line {line_core}), so it is never "
"applied: move it just after \"RewriteEngine On\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/Stdlib/HtaccessAudit.php:150
msgid ""
"The files \"{type}\" are redirected to the module Analytics (line {line}) "
"before the module Access (line {line_access}): the protection of these files "
"is bypassed. Place the rule of Access first."
msgstr ""

#: src/Stdlib/HtaccessAudit.php:156
msgid ""
"The files \"{type}\" are redirected to the module {module} (line {line}), so "
"the rule of the module {module_2} (line {line_2}) is not used for them."
msgstr ""

